{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02969",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.33,
      "end_seconds": 4.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.72,
      "end_seconds": 9.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.35,
      "end_seconds": 15.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got a sudden high fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.35,
      "end_seconds": 22.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Right, can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.46,
      "end_seconds": 27.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "I take sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.69,
      "end_seconds": 47.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.29,
      "end_seconds": 62.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "Just since yesterday. I've been putting this off for weeks. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.3,
      "end_seconds": 65.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.7,
      "end_seconds": 68.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Honestly, every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.23,
      "end_seconds": 73.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.07,
      "end_seconds": 91.31,
      "duration_seconds": 17.24,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get vomiting and diarrhoea as well. Oh, the vomiting and diarrhoea? That's been for two days. With vomiting and diarrhoea, it's on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.25,
      "end_seconds": 104.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "And what about sore throat, stiff neck or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.58,
      "end_seconds": 109.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Erm, um, no, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.06,
      "end_seconds": 112.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.62,
      "end_seconds": 116.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.92,
      "end_seconds": 124.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Okay, any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.03,
      "end_seconds": 129.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.69,
      "end_seconds": 137.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "So, tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.34,
      "end_seconds": 152.5,
      "duration_seconds": 11.16,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. I grab fast food at lunch most days. I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.3,
      "end_seconds": 159.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.52,
      "end_seconds": 166.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I've had migraines for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.34,
      "end_seconds": 171.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Alright, are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.01,
      "end_seconds": 174.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Uh, my cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.34,
      "end_seconds": 179.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.11,
      "end_seconds": 193.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.92,
      "end_seconds": 213.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 100 over 56, heart rate 108, saturation 96 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.38,
      "end_seconds": 219.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Okay, shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.11,
      "end_seconds": 222.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.85,
      "end_seconds": 225.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.72,
      "end_seconds": 249.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.83,
      "text": "You are very hot, your blood pressure is low and there is a flat red rash over the body and palms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.9,
      "end_seconds": 256.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.37,
      "end_seconds": 279.47,
      "duration_seconds": 11.1,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. It's hard to say. Possible toxic shock syndrome is one possibility and a viral illness another, and I'd rather not commit yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.06,
      "end_seconds": 286.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Okay, so will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.53,
      "end_seconds": 296.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.04,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like possible toxic shock syndrome, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.77,
      "end_seconds": 343.26,
      "duration_seconds": 32.49,
      "text": "I'll request a vaginal swab, it'll help with possible toxic shock. The treatment will be flucloxacillin, 2 grams, now, single dose. That should help with possible toxic shock syndrome. Remove any tampon, you are going to hospital now. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Okay, have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.09,
      "end_seconds": 347.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Oh, thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.95,
      "end_seconds": 350.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}